    "non_hurst_rs": "Hurst/RS is rescaled-range (R/S) / long-memory scaling of cumulative deviations. HFD is Higuchi curve-length scaling of the series itself; different estimator and phenomenon.",
    "non_entropy_vs_Shannon_perm_sample_Renyi2_spectral": "Entropy families are distribution/information measures (p*log p, ordinal pattern frequencies, template matches, PSD bin probs). HFD is geometric multi-scale curve-length scaling \u2014 not an information measure.",
